      "adoption": "Historical incidents for non-China companies may proceed when contained and remediated; current unresolved issues remain held.",
      "usefulness": "Automate build and session GETs provide cheap authenticated inventory of test runs without billed live-browser sessions.",
      "incident": "On 9 November 2014 BrowserStack reported unauthorized access via Shellshock on an inactive legacy prototype server; a partial list of registered email addresses was accessed and misleading emails reached fewer than 1% of registered users. Status fully resolved 10 November 2014. April 2026 public reporting that a unique BrowserStack-only canary email received targeted spam is unconfirmed by BrowserStack and is not treated as a current unresolved platform compromise. CVE-2026-48723 (browserstack-cypress-cli <= 1.36.3 command injection) was patched in 1.36.4 and is a local CLI issue, not an Automate REST API breach.",
      "remediation": "BrowserStack published a 10 November 2014 incident report, took the prototype server offline, and later documented SOC 2 Type II / ISO 27001:2022 controls. The cypress-cli advisory was patched in 1.36.4 on 22 May 2026.",
      "residualRisk": "Historical email-list exposure from 2014 and unconfirmed 2026 canary-email spam remain residual. Live authentication unverified.",
